caption: Experience Loop
tradition-component: experience-loop

Choose one loop. Awards are Active Martial Experience, use the campaign's active martial award limits, and share the Tier 2 lifetime cap of 500 character points.

Justicar's Road — Requires Code of Honor (Xia). Gain 0.2 XP for defeating a qualifying ordinary bandit or tyrant's minion, 1 XP for an elite, and 1-5 XP for a tyrant. Ordinary means below 25% of your current CP; elite means at least 25%. A tyrant personally exercises coercive authority through an abusive system; award 1 XP, +1 per full tenfold increase above 100 subjects, maximum 5. Genuine reform with meaningful restitution grants the same award again, but that reform bonus is revoked as debt if the tyrant willingly returns to tyranny. Defeat includes incapacitation, capture, surrender, rout, or genuine reform. The stylist must be principally responsible. Staged crimes and cultivated enemies do not qualify. A genuinely returned offender may qualify again.

Unseen Hand — Gain 1 XP for completing a consequential infiltration, manipulation, theft, rescue, or assassination objective without the target or opposing organization correctly identifying you as responsible before completion. Repeated objectives against the same target require materially changed circumstances. Staged, reversible, or trivial operations do not qualify.

Worthy Rival — Gain 5 XP for defeating an opponent who previously defeated you in earnest combat. They cease to be Worthy after you defeat them until they materially improve, such as gaining an Attribute, Duan Wei, +5 in a primary combat skill, or a major equipment upgrade. Staged victories do not qualify. Total XP gained from one rival can never exceed one fifth of that rival's CP value.

Hundredfold Tempering (百炼成钢) — Gain 1 XP per 25 HP of injury actually suffered in lethal combat against serious enemies. Count injury after DR and Injury Tolerance. Sparring, trivial opposition, self-inflicted injury, and arranged friendly injury do not qualify. Qualifying injury accumulates across combats and is counted once when suffered.

Closed-Door Furnace (闭关苦修) — Generation Basis: Training / Recovery Burden. Gain 1 XP per 1,200 FP actually spent on deliberate Style training and subsequently recovered naturally. Qualifying burden includes exhausting forms, stance training, weapon drills, breath work, weighted practice, and comparable intentional cultivation. Ordinary combat, travel, environmental fatigue, deprivation, and incidental FP expenditure do not qualify. FP that was never spent because a maneuver or ability costs no FP cannot count. Qualifying FP accumulates across training sessions and is counted once when spent.

Challenge the Heavens — Generation Basis: Quest / Adventure Accomplishment. Gain XP for defeating an opponent substantially stronger than yourself in earnest combat: 1 XP if the opponent is at least 125% of your current CP, 2 XP at 150%, 3 XP at 200%, 4 XP at 300%, and 5 XP at 400% or more. Use the highest threshold reached, not cumulative thresholds. The opponent must be genuine opposition and you must be principally responsible for the victory. Each opponent qualifies only once until they materially improve. Staged fights, cooperative opponents, and deliberately inflated CP totals do not qualify.

Ten Thousand Schools — Generation Basis: Quest / Adventure Accomplishment. The first time you defeat a consequential practitioner of a distinct institutional martial Style or Jutsu tree in earnest combat, gain 1 XP. If you later defeat a genuine master of that same lineage, increase the lifetime award from that lineage to 3 XP total. A genuine master means a character who has actually achieved the lineage's Mastery or an explicitly equivalent capstone status. Cosmetic variants, deliberately created splinter schools, renamed copies, and trivial derivative lineages do not count separately. The practitioner must meaningfully demonstrate the lineage during the qualifying encounter.

Tournament Road — Generation Basis: Quest / Adventure Accomplishment. Gain 1 XP for winning a meaningful local martial tournament, 2-3 XP for winning a substantial regional or elite tournament, and 4-5 XP for winning a major international, interworld, or campaign-level tournament. The event must involve genuine competitive uncertainty and serious opposition. Staged brackets, hired entrants, trivial micro-tournaments, and events designed primarily to feed the loop do not qualify. A recurring tournament may qualify again only when the field, stakes, or competitive circumstances have materially changed.

The Wandering Sword — Generation Basis: Quest / Adventure Accomplishment. Gain 1-5 XP when you enter a community in which you have no preexisting authority or responsibility and resolve a consequential local problem before moving on. Use the normal Quest / Adventure scale: 1 XP for a minor but meaningful accomplishment, 2-3 XP for a substantial accomplishment, and 4-5 XP for a major campaign objective. Examples include escorting endangered travelers, settling a clan feud, defeating a dangerous local foe, recovering a stolen heirloom, rescuing captives, or ending a threat to the community. The same community does not qualify again without materially changed circumstances, and trivial or manufactured problems do not qualify.

Debts of the Jianghu — Generation Basis: Quest / Adventure Accomplishment. Gain 1-5 XP for conclusively discharging a serious personal debt of gratitude, vengeance, honor, or obligation accepted under the Style's ethos. Use 1 XP for a minor but consequential debt, 2-3 XP for a substantial debt involving real danger, sacrifice, or lasting consequence, and 4-5 XP for a defining life-debt, clan-scale obligation, or comparable major undertaking. The debt must arise from genuine events or obligations rather than a cooperative exchange created to feed the loop. A debt awards only once when actually discharged.

The Lost Manual — Generation Basis: Quest / Adventure Accomplishment. Gain 1 XP for recovering, deciphering, reconstructing, or proving authentic a meaningful lost martial fragment or secret technique; 2-3 XP for restoring a substantial lost curriculum or manual; and 4-5 XP for restoring a legendary, effectively extinct, or campaign-significant martial lineage. Each body of lore awards only once. Copies, translations of already recovered material, staged rediscovery, and materially redundant fragments do not qualify. Any actual access to the recovered martial material is a separate fictional benefit and does not increase the XP award.

Blood-Red Ascension — Generation Basis: Blood Sacrifice. After personally defeating a consequential martial practitioner in earnest combat, the stylist may perform a genuine ritual sacrifice of that defeated practitioner according to the Style's fixed method. Gain 1 XP per full 100 CP of the victim, minimum 1 and maximum 5 XP. The victim must be at least 25% of the stylist's current CP and must actually possess meaningful martial training or supernatural martial capability. Each victim can qualify only once. Captives acquired through staged combat, cooperative victims, mass executions, ordinary noncombatants, and sacrifices performed only to farm XP do not qualify. A Style that selects this loop should carry a fixed Shido compatible with deliberate ritual killing.

Warrior's Crucible — Generation Basis: Training / Recovery Burden. Gain 1 XP per 600 FP actually spent during earnest combat against serious opposition on martial Extra Effort, FP-costing combat maneuvers, cinematic martial skills or techniques, or Shadow Arts Jutsu. Only FP actually paid by the practitioner counts; waived, reduced, substituted, or merely nominal costs do not. Qualifying FP must actually have been lost from the practitioner's FP pool. Fit, Very Fit, Regeneration (Fatigue Only), and other legitimate recovery abilities may restore it normally; accelerated recovery does not invalidate the expenditure. The same FP can qualify again only after it has actually been restored and spent again in a later qualifying expenditure. FP spent on unrelated supernatural powers, environmental hardship, travel, deprivation, enemy-imposed fatigue, or staged or trivial combat does not qualify. Qualifying expenditure accumulates across combats. Effortless Grace may reduce or eliminate otherwise qualifying FP costs; FP not actually spent generates no XP.
